---
title: "A row's life"
config:
  markdownAutoWrap: false
  state:
    useMaxWidth: false
---
stateDiagram-v2
  classDef plain fill:#f4f6f7,stroke:#566573,color:#1b2631
  classDef group0 fill:#fdebd0,stroke:#7f7668,color:#1b2631
  classDef group1 fill:#d6eaf8,stroke:#6b757c,color:#1b2631
  classDef group2 fill:#d1f2eb,stroke:#697976,color:#1b2631
  classDef group3 fill:#e5e8e8,stroke:#737474,color:#1b2631
  state "Legend" as legend {
    state "Not launched" as legendGroup0
    state "Launched" as legendGroup1
    state "Final" as legendGroup2
    state "Removed" as legendGroup3
  }
  class legendGroup0 group0
  class legendGroup1 group1
  class legendGroup2 group2
  class legendGroup3 group3
  state "At the same time" as regions {
    state "The go" as region0 {
      [*] --> r0s3
      state "Approved" as r0s0
      state "Held" as r0s1
      state "Held, its go kept" as r0s2
      state "No go" as r0s3
      r0s0 --> r0s3 : its go no longer holds, and it<br/>waits for yours [when gate (a<br/>question is open) or queued<br/>(no thread yet)]
      %% when r1s2, r1s7
      r0s0 --> r0s1 : you hold the approved row
      r0s0 --> r0s2 : you hold the row, keeping its<br/>go
      r0s1 --> r0s0 : you approve the held row, and<br/>the hold ends
      r0s2 --> r0s0 : you approve the row over the<br/>hold that kept its go
      r0s2 --> r0s0 : you lift the hold, and its go<br/>comes back
      r0s3 --> r0s0 : you approve the row, or a rule<br/>gives its go
      r0s3 --> r0s1 : you hold the row
    }
    --
    state "The row's status" as region1 {
      [*] --> r1s7
      state "done (a clean Result from<br/>a thread that ended)" as r1s0
      state "failed (the thread failed)" as r1s1
      state "gate (a question is open)" as r1s2
      state "launched (a launch with no<br/>thread yet)" as r1s3
      state "left (the Result leaves<br/>work)" as r1s4
      state "merged (its pull request<br/>merged)" as r1s5
      state "pr (its pull request is<br/>open)" as r1s6
      state "queued (no thread yet)" as r1s7
      state "removed (queue.py<br/>`remove`, no pass sets it)" as r1s8
      state "running (the thread at<br/>work, a Result or not, or<br/>its pull request opening)" as r1s9
      state "stale (the thread ended<br/>with nothing written)" as r1s10
      state "waiting (the thread asks<br/>you)" as r1s11
      r1s0 --> r1s5 : the pull request of a done row<br/>merges on your accept
      r1s1 --> r1s0 : a Result says done after the<br/>thread failed
      r1s1 --> r1s4 : the failed thread leaves its<br/>work to its home
      r1s1 --> r1s9 : the failed thread works again
      r1s2 --> r1s11 : the question closes
      r1s2 --> r1s1 : the question closes
      r1s2 --> r1s9 : the question closes
      r1s2 --> r1s10 : the question closes
      r1s2 --> r1s4 : the question closes
      r1s2 --> r1s7 : the question closes, and the<br/>row's launch has no record
      r1s2 --> r1s3 : the question closes, and the<br/>row's launch has no thread yet
      r1s2 --> r1s6 : the question closes, and the<br/>row's pull request is open
      r1s2 --> r1s5 : the question closes, and the<br/>row's pull request merged
      r1s2 --> r1s0 : the question closes, and the<br/>row's Result says done
      r1s3 --> r1s2 : jbus opens a question
      r1s3 --> r1s9 : T3 Code lists the thread at<br/>work
      r1s3 --> r1s5 : the pull request merges
      r1s3 --> r1s6 : the pull request opens
      r1s3 --> r1s11 : the thread asks for an answer
      r1s3 --> r1s10 : the thread ends
      r1s3 --> r1s0 : the thread ends with a clean<br/>Result before a pass sees it<br/>at work
      r1s3 --> r1s4 : the thread ends with work left<br/>before a pass sees it at work
      r1s3 --> r1s1 : the thread fails before a pass<br/>sees it at work
      r1s4 --> r1s0 : a follow-up Result says done
      r1s4 --> r1s6 : a pull request opens for what<br/>was left
      r1s4 --> r1s3 : jbus launches the row again<br/>for what was left
      r1s4 --> r1s11 : the thread asks for an answer<br/>again
      r1s4 --> r1s9 : the thread works again on what<br/>was left
      r1s4 --> r1s8 : you remove the row from left
      r1s6 --> r1s2 : jbus opens a question on the<br/>row with its pull request open
      r1s6 --> r1s4 : the pull request closes<br/>unmerged
      r1s6 --> r1s8 : you remove the row from pr
      r1s7 --> r1s3 : a launch record names a thread<br/>for the row [when Approved]
      %% when r0s0
      r1s7 --> r1s2 : jbus opens a question on the<br/>row
      r1s7 --> r1s8 : you remove the row from queued
      r1s9 --> r1s6 : a pull request opens
      r1s9 --> r1s3 : the crew opens nothing after<br/>its review
      r1s9 --> r1s5 : the pull request opens and<br/>merges between two passes
      r1s9 --> r1s4 : the Result leaves work, or the<br/>pull request closes
      r1s9 --> r1s11 : the thread asks for an answer<br/>to its request
      r1s9 --> r1s0 : the thread ends with a clean<br/>Result and no pull request
      r1s9 --> r1s1 : the thread fails
      r1s9 --> r1s10 : the turn hangs, or the thread<br/>ends with nothing written
      r1s10 --> r1s0 : the crew writes a clean Result
      r1s10 --> r1s4 : the thread stays quiet with<br/>nothing written, or writes a<br/>leftover
      r1s10 --> r1s9 : the thread works again
      r1s11 --> r1s3 : T3 Code lists no thread
      r1s11 --> r1s9 : the request is answered and<br/>the thread works again
      r1s11 --> r1s4 : the thread ends after its<br/>request with work left
      r1s11 --> r1s1 : the thread fails while it<br/>waits
      r1s11 --> r1s3 : the thread starts
    }
  }
  class r0s0 plain
  class r0s1 plain
  class r0s2 plain
  class r0s3 plain
  class r1s0 group2
  class r1s1 group1
  class r1s2 group0
  class r1s3 group1
  class r1s4 group1
  class r1s5 group2
  class r1s6 group1
  class r1s7 group0
  class r1s8 group3
  class r1s9 group1
  class r1s10 group1
  class r1s11 group1
